{
  "_comment": "Mixed registry: local models via a native Ollama install (host.docker.internal, no containerized `ollama` service needed) alongside the hosted OpenAI and Gemini providers, so a consensus run fans out across all of them. Ollama model_key values match one machine's `ollama list` output -- swap for whatever you actually have pulled. OpenAI/Gemini need OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY set in .env. Ids only need to match ANALYZER_MODEL_ID / JUDGE_MODEL_ID / CONSENSUS_MODEL_ID in .env. gemini-flash-latest is Google's rolling alias for their current default model -- pinning a dated snapshot (e.g. gemini-1.5-pro, gemini-2.5-pro) risks it being retired later, which is exactly what happened when this file was first written. Gemini cost_per_1k values are a rough estimate, not pulled from a live pricing endpoint -- check Google's current rate card if accurate cost tracking matters.",
